esp32s31 SMP parity: per-hart idle policy; hosted-HID attach before the HID bus

Files (whole): arch/riscv/kernel/process.c, drivers/hid/esp32s31-hosted-hid.c
(patches/0051's CLIC driver refreshed: global poll and the false "hart0
frozen" panic removed).

process.c arch_cpu_idle(): with a second CPU online hart 1 does not wfi (a
cross-hart pending bit does not wake it) and returns; the lent CPU DOES wfi -
it traps to the hart0 monitor, which leaves the exception and blocks in
FreeRTOS until something is pending. Replaces cpu_idle_poll_ctrl(true), which
made the lent CPU spin 460,000 traps/s on the shared bus (gate canaries +11%)
and starved hart0's IDLE task.

esp32s31-hosted-hid.c: hid_add_device() -EINVAL (HID bus not registered yet)
re-queues the attach every 100 ms, up to 10 s. On an SMP boot hart0's attach
beat hid_init() and the keyboard and mouse were lost for the whole boot.
